 6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 9-3\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =18-18 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102755/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0272b8d6-8400-5a6d-b51d-fc6ca84bd166"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102755"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-69915"] :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-0\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
